# Wikicrop tools - files a checkout creates when the tools run.
# The repository holds the tools only: no project data, sheet content, logs or personal settings.

### Personal settings and credentials ###
# Copy settings.example.toml to settings.local.toml and fill it in: it stays on your machine.
scripts/settings.*.toml
!scripts/settings.example.toml
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
# pywikibot, if used beside these tools
user-config.py
user-password.py
throttle.ctrl
apicache*/

### Project data (settings defaults, under the repository root) ###
data/
Crops/
working documents/

### Data files of any kind: sheet snapshots, source workbooks, logs, review tables ###
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.ods
*.csv
*.tsv

### Sheet-varieties: blocks built from real sheet content ###
# Only the example drafts module and the template ship.
scripts/sheet-varieties/table3_block_*_drafts.py
!scripts/sheet-varieties/table3_block_example_drafts.py
scripts/sheet-varieties/fill_table3_block_*.gs
scripts/sheet-varieties/mock/grid*.json
scripts/sheet-varieties/mock/mock_after*.json
scripts/sheet-varieties/mock/mock_log.txt

### Source finder cache and output ###
scripts/source-finder/.cache/
scripts/source-finder/out/

### Video transcripts: media and transcripts stay private (see video-transcript/README.md) ###
*.mp4
*.m4a
*.mp3
*.wav
*.webm
*.mkv
*-transcript.md

### Document export output ###
*.odt
*.pdf
*.wiki

### Python and Node ###
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
node_modules/

### Packaging marker ###
.wikicrop-submission

### IDEs and OS ###
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
*.ipr
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
